14
00:00:46.983 --> 00:00:50.541
Your turn. Say: Relaxation technique.

15
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.144
Relaxation technique.

16
00:00:55.883 --> 00:00:56.826
Deep breathing.

17
00:00:57.817 --> 00:01:00.455
Deep breathing means taking slow, full breaths.

18
00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.875
Deep breathing slows my heartbeat.

19
00:01:03.483 --> 00:01:06.066
Your turn. Say: Deep breathing.

20
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:10.006
Deep breathing.

21
00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:11.960
Time pressure.

22
00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:15.948
Time pressure means stress from having little time.

23
00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.468
Time pressure makes me nervous.

24
00:01:19.083 --> 00:01:21.770
Your turn. Say: Time pressure.

25
00:01:24.633 --> 00:01:25.809
Time pressure.

26
00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:27.516
Overwhelm.

27
00:01:28.517 --> 00:01:32.652
Overwhelm means to give someone too many feelings or tasks at once.

28
00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:35.668
Too much homework can overwhelm students.

29
00:01:36.283 --> 00:01:38.738
Your turn. Say: Overwhelm.

30
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:42.682
Overwhelm.

31
00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:44.720
Coping mechanism.

32
00:01:45.717 --> 00:01:48.842
Coping mechanism means a way to deal with difficulty.

33
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.345
Drawing is my coping mechanism.

34
00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:54.811
Your turn. Say: Coping mechanism.

35
00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:59.028
Coping mechanism.

36
00:01:59.783 --> 00:02:00.657
Journaling.

37
00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:04.393
Journaling means writing your thoughts in a diary.

38
00:02:04.983 --> 00:02:07.436
Journaling helps me understand my feelings.

39
00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.366
Your turn. Say: Journaling.

40
00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.097
Journaling.

41
00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:16.165
Physical activity.

42
00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:21.135
Physical activity means moving your body, like sport or walking.

43
00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.144
Physical activity reduces stress.

44
00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.600
Your turn. Say: Physical activity.

45
00:02:30.433 --> 00:02:31.841
Physical activity.

46
00:02:32.583 --> 00:02:33.851
Support system.

47
00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:37.349
Support system means the people who help you.

48
00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.019
My family is my support system.

49
00:02:40.617 --> 00:02:43.269
Your turn. Say: Support system.

50
00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:47.610
Support system.

51
00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.607
Mindful breathing.

52
00:02:50.617 --> 00:02:53.661
Mindful breathing means noticing each breath calmly.

53
00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:57.178
Mindful breathing helps me focus before tests.

54
00:02:57.783 --> 00:03:00.947
Your turn. Say: Mindful breathing.

55
00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.173
Mindful breathing.

56
00:03:05.917 --> 00:03:07.104
Resilience.

57
00:03:08.117 --> 00:03:11.324
Resilience means the ability to recover from problems.

58
00:03:11.917 --> 00:03:14.125
Resilience grows with every challenge.

59
00:03:14.717 --> 00:03:17.265
Your turn. Say: Resilience.

60
00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.322
Resilience.

61
00:03:22.083 --> 00:03:23.769
Self-regulate.

62
00:03:24.783 --> 00:03:27.955
Self-regulate means to control your own feelings.

63
00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:31.490
Good sleep helps teenagers self-regulate.

64
00:03:32.083 --> 00:03:34.689
Your turn. Say: Self-regulate.

65
00:03:37.533 --> 00:03:38.987
Self-regulate.

66
00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:43.637
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:44.483 --> 00:03:47.876
Visal, what relaxation technique helps you manage stress?

68
00:03:48.983 --> 00:03:52.794
Whenever I feel stressed, I practice deep breathing.

69
00:03:53.883 --> 00:03:55.778
What are your stress triggers?

70
00:03:56.883 --> 00:04:01.904
Time pressure. Whenever I have three deadlines, I feel overwhelmed.

71
00:04:03.017 --> 00:04:04.296
What else helps?

72
00:04:05.383 --> 00:04:09.510
Journaling. Whenever I write my thoughts down, I feel calmer.

73
00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:12.225
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:13.083 --> 00:04:16.047
Grammar focus: Whenever and whenever clauses.

75
00:04:16.347 --> 00:04:17.429
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:18.117 --> 00:04:20.848
Whenever I feel stressed, I practice deep breathing.

77
00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:24.388
Whenever I have a test, I go to bed early.

78
00:04:25.283 --> 00:04:27.991
I write in my journal whenever I feel sad.

79
00:04:28.933 --> 00:04:33.699
'Whenever' means 'every time'. Use the present simple in both parts for habits.

80
00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:39.378
Be careful! Don't say: Whenever I will feel stressed, I breathe deeply.

81
00:04:41.333 --> 00:04:44.343
Say: Whenever I feel stressed, I breathe deeply.

82
00:04:44.643 --> 00:04:46.921
Use the present simple after 'whenever'.

83
00:04:47.733 --> 00:04:50.560
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:51.367 --> 00:04:52.646
Calm Under Pressure.

85
00:04:52.946 --> 00:04:56.560
Everyone has stress triggers, like time pressure or exams.

86
00:04:57.567 --> 00:05:00.344
Deep breathing and journaling help me self-regulate.

87
00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:04.714
Whenever I feel overwhelmed, I take a short walk.

88
00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.988
Physical activity and a good support system also help.

89
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.579
Recognizing my stress triggers builds resilience over time.

90
00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:18.355
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:19.217 --> 00:05:21.437
blank I feel stressed, I breathe deeply.

92
00:05:21.737 --> 00:05:25.506
A, Whenever. B, Wherever. C, However.

93
00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:30.985
The answer is A: Whenever.

94
00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:34.614
Something that causes a feeling is a blank.

95
00:05:34.914 --> 00:05:38.138
A, trigger. B, technique. C, system.

96
00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.943
The answer is A: trigger.

97
00:05:45.083 --> 00:05:47.826
The ability to recover from problems is blank.

98
00:05:48.126 --> 00:05:52.488
A, resilience. B, overwhelm. C, pressure.

99
00:05:56.033 --> 00:05:58.358
The answer is A: resilience.

100
00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:02.625
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:03.483 --> 00:06:06.505
What relaxation technique helps you manage stress?

102
00:06:15.317 --> 00:06:16.712
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:17.012 --> 00:06:24.831
Whenever I feel stressed, I listen to calm music and breathe slowly. Whenever I have too much homework, I make a list.

104
00:06:25.131 --> 00:06:26.841
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:32.643
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and whenever and whenever clauses.

106
00:06:32.943 --> 00:06:37.047
Today's value is self-care. Look after yourself and rest when you are sick.

107
00:06:37.347 --> 00:06:39.964
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:40.264 --> 00:06:43.160
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

